From aaa52f8e1e36e2673344be4164d149733a3f3cb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: minhmc2007 <quangminh21072010@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:33:25 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] FaceUnlock: drop the arm64-only Megvii prebuilts from
 required

  TARGET module FaceUnlock requires non-existent TARGET module:
    libFaceDetectCA
  ... 3 more
  build/make/core/main.mk:506: error: Build failed.

The four Megvii prebuilts declare only android_arm64 srcs, so soong emits
no variant on x86_64 and kati fails the required-deps check at
main.mk:497.

TARGET_FACE_UNLOCK_SUPPORTED cannot reach this. It keeps FaceUnlock out
of PRODUCT_PACKAGES via packages/apps/FaceUnlock/common.mk, but
frameworks/base/services/core statically requires
vendor.aospa.biometrics.face, whose source lives in this project. That
keeps the namespace in ALL_MODULES regardless of what is installed, and
the check at main.mk:439 iterates ALL_MODULES, so the deps are validated
even when the app is not built.

The four modules stay defined below, just unreferenced. Gating the
services/core dependency on a product variable would be the real fix.

205 patches, 0 conflicts.
---
 Android.bp | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 82a72ca..46e8491 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -25,11 +25,14 @@ android_app {
         "vendor.aospa.biometrics.face.impl",
     ],
 
+    // libFaceDetectCA, libmegface_faceunlock, libMegviiUnlock and
+    // libMegviiUnlock-jni-1.2 are still defined below, but they declare
+    // only android_arm64 srcs. Requiring them on any other arch fails kati
+    // with "requires non-existent TARGET module" even though this app is
+    // not installed, because frameworks/base hardcodes a dependency on
+    // vendor.aospa.biometrics.face, which keeps the namespace -- and so
+    // this module's required deps -- in ALL_MODULES.
     required: [
-        "libFaceDetectCA",
-        "libmegface_faceunlock",
-        "libMegviiUnlock",
-        "libMegviiUnlock-jni-1.2",
         "default_permissions_co.aospa.sense.xml",
         "hiddenapi-whitelist-co.aospa.sense.xml",
         "privapp_whitelist_co.aospa.sense.xml",
